# IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION FOR WOMEN AND CHILDREN FROM VIOLENCE

MAYOR OF METRO

LAMPUNG PROVINCE

# REGIONAL REGULATION OF METRO CITY

NUMBER 03 OF 2014

CONCERNING

IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION FOR WOMEN AND CHILDREN FROM VIOLENCE

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD

MAYOR OF METRO,

Considering:







a. that within every human being are inherent human rights that must be respected, upheld and protected by the state, law, Regional Government and every person for the sake of honor and protection of human dignity and worth;
b. that women and children are among vulnerable groups who tend to become victims of violence and crimes against humanity which constitute violations of human rights, thus requiring protection through regulations that can provide prevention and protection for victims of violence;
c. that based on Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection and Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence, the Regional Government together with the community is obligated to undertake prevention, protection, and recovery efforts for victims of violence;
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letters a, b, and c above, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Implementation of Protection for Women and Children from Violence;

In View of:







1. Law Number 7 of 1984 concerning Ratification of the Convention on The Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1984 Number 29, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3277);
2. Law Number 5 of 1998 concerning Ratification of the Convention Against Torture and Other Cruel, Inhuman or Degrading Treatment or Punishment (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1998 Number 164, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3783);
3. Law Number 12 of 1999 concerning the Establishment of Level II Regency of Way Kanan, Level II Regency of East Lampung and Level II Municipality of Metro (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 46, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3825);
4. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);
5. Law Number 1 of 2000 concerning Ratification of ILO Convention No. 182 Concerning The Prohibition and Immediate Action of The Worst Forms of Child Labour (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2000 Number 30, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3941);
6. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);
7. Law Number 32 of 2004 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 125, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4437) as amended several times most recently by Law Number 12 of 2008 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2008 Number 59, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4844);
8. Law Number 36 of 2009 concerning Health (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2009 Number 44, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5063);
9. Law Number 12 of 2011 concerning the Formulation of Legislation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2011 Number 82, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5234);
10. Law Number 16 of 2011 concerning Legal Aid (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2011 Number 104, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5248);
11. Law Number 10 of 2012 concerning Ratification of the Optional Protocol to The Convention on The Rights of The Child on The Sale of Children, Child Prostitution and Child Pornography (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2012 Number 149, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5330);
12. Law Number 11 of 2012 concerning the Juvenile Criminal Justice System (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2012 Number 153, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5332);
13. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning Implementation and Cooperation for Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4604);
14. Government Regulation Number 38 of 2007 concerning Division of Governmental Affairs between the Government, Provincial Regional Government and Regency/Municipal Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2007 Number 82);
15. Presidential Regulation Number 1 of 2007 concerning Ratification, Promulgation, and Dissemination of Legislation;
16. Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 1 of 2014 concerning the Formulation of Regional Legal Products (State News of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 32);
17. Regional Regulation of Metro City Number 6 of 2008 concerning Governmental Affairs that are the Authority of the Regional Government of Metro City (Regional Gazette of Metro City of 2008 Number 06, Supplement to the Regional Gazette of Metro City Number 106);
18. Regional Regulation of Metro City Number 7 of 2008 concerning the Establishment of Organization and Working Procedures of Regional Apparatus of Metro City (Regional Gazette of Metro City of 2008 Number 07, Supplement to the Regional Gazette of Metro City Number 107) as amended by Regional Regulation of Metro City Number 12 of 2010 (Regional Gazette of Metro City of 2012 Number 01, Supplement to the Regional Gazette of Metro City Number 01);
19. Regional Regulation of Metro City Number 6 of 2013 concerning Implementation of Legal Aid (Regional Gazette of Metro City of 2013 Number 03, Supplement to the Regional Gazette of Metro City Number 03);

With Mutual Approval

REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF METRO CITY

and

MAYOR OF METRO

